# Lab 03 - Tiny Transformer Language Model

## Objective
The objective of this lab was to understand how Transformer-based language models work by building and training a small Transformer model for text generation.

## Tasks Completed
- Loaded and explored the TinyStories dataset
- Preprocessed and tokenized text data
- Prepared input and target sequences
- Implemented a Tiny Transformer architecture
- Trained the model for next-token prediction
- Evaluated model performance using loss and perplexity
- Generated text from a given prompt
- Saved the trained model for future use

## Tools and Libraries
- Python
- PyTorch
- Transformers
- NumPy
- Matplotlib

## Learning Outcomes
Through this lab, I gained practical experience in building and training a Transformer-based language model. I learned how token embeddings, positional embeddings, self-attention, feed-forward networks, and loss functions work together to generate text. I also understood the impact of model parameters on training performance and generated outputs.

